            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "MaryBello"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very delicious! I had about 4 large yellow potatoes, and a bunch of carrots that needed to be used. So my soup was more carroty and less potato-y than this version, but it worked. I also prepared about 1 lb. of shredded chicken in the crockpot earlier in the day, and added the shredded chicken to the soup at the same stage that I added the cheddar.",
            "datePublished": "2020-04-26T01:57:14.580Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "loria"
            },
            "reviewBody": "I like anything that I can make in 1 pot (and I have an immersion mixer, so I didn't have to transfer half to the blender). I didn't have enough broth, so I had to use some water &amp; I didn't have a lot of cheese so I don't know how much I used. Other than that, I left the recipe simple. It was easy to make, it was easy to eat, and it was much better than the last carrot soup recipe I tried. I should have cooked it a little bit longer because I like my carrots a little softer.",
            "datePublished": "2013-10-23T17:15:58.320Z"
